# Options no OpenSigner image builds, whatever it runs on. A symbol here
# takes everything under it: NET alone removes INET, IPV6, netfilter, the
# wireless and Bluetooth stacks and every network driver.
#
# What one device forbids and another needs is not here. It is in that
# board's own kernel.forbidden or kernel.required.

MODULES        a loadable module is a driver that is not in the image and can still be loaded into it
NET            the device signs offline; with no socket layer there is no interface, no stack and no driver to reach one
INET           follows NET, and named on its own so a stack cannot come back under a different menu
WLAN           no radios
BT             no radios
SOUND          the device has no speaker and the app makes no sound
DRM            the firmware hands Linux a plain framebuffer; the kernel-mode-setting stack draws nothing here
USB_GADGET     a device-mode USB port is a way into the device that nothing in this image needs
INPUT_JOYSTICK nothing in this product is played
INPUT_MISC     nothing behind it is on any of these devices
RC_CORE        no infrared receiver
DVB_CORE       no tuner
IIO            no sensors
MD             no array; the medium is one device
MTD            no flash chip, and BLOCK2MTD would make the boot medium into one
SWAP           a page holding a seed must have nowhere to be written to
DEVMEM         /dev/mem is all of physical memory, the peripherals included
KEXEC          loading a second kernel over this one keeps the device running a kernel that is not on the medium
MAGIC_SYSRQ    no input device may reboot the device, kill the app or dump kernel state
DEBUG_FS       debugfs publishes kernel internals as a writable filesystem
PROC_KCORE     /proc/kcore is the running kernel's memory as a file to read
EXT4_FS        the rootfs is an initramfs and the exchange partition is FAT; no other filesystem is ever mounted
BTRFS_FS       as EXT4_FS
F2FS_FS        as EXT4_FS
XFS_FS         as EXT4_FS
NFS_FS         a network filesystem on a device with no network
CIFS           as NFS_FS
SQUASHFS       nothing on the medium is an image to loop-mount
OVERLAY_FS     nothing is layered over the read-only root
FUSE_FS        no filesystem is implemented in userspace here
BLK_DEV_LOOP   a file must not become a block device
BLK_DEV_NBD    a block device over a network the kernel does not have
BLK_DEV_RAM    the rootfs is linked into the kernel; /dev/ram* has no use
CRYPTO_USER_API the app carries its own curve and hashes; the kernel's crypto has no user
PROFILING      a profiler reads what the app is doing
KPROBES        a probe rewrites kernel text at runtime
FTRACE         a trace of every call on a device that signs
BPF_SYSCALL    loadable programs in the kernel, which is what MODULES is out for
NAMESPACES     one program, one namespace
CGROUPS        nothing is being limited or accounted for
AUDIT          nothing collects an audit log and there is nowhere to send one
SUSPEND        the device is on or it is off; a suspended device holds a seed in DRAM with nobody watching
HIBERNATION    hibernation writes memory to storage, which is the one thing a seed must never do
EEPROM_AT24    a driver that can write a small non-volatile chip has no use here
EEPROM_AT25    as EEPROM_AT24
EEPROM_93CX6   as EEPROM_AT24
NVMEM_SYSFS    the sysfs faces of the nvmem providers, which are writable
KGDB           a kernel debugger on the serial port of a device that signs; it also selects MAGIC_SYSRQ
